  "verified": "Year 1 comprises eight required courses, 60 EC. Year 2 is 55 required EC and one 5 EC choice, instantiated as first-listed Healthy Ageing independently of UCR fit. Year 3 is 30 choice EC, one split 15 EC project and three 5 EC courses. Both Landscapes and Fieldwork Abroad include essential fieldwork. Statistics 1 precedes Statistics 2. Statistics 1 and Introduction to Academic Research precede Quantitative Research Methods. GIS and the year-two methods courses precede the project. Fieldwork Abroad needs 90 of the first 120 EC by September 1. The regular sequence meets these conditions. Course descriptions support distinguishing disciplinary geography from general thematic parallels.",
